{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Operator-authorised production deploy of the nginx half of this fix — DONE and verified live (2026-08-27 ~22:05 UTC).\n\n## The substitution mechanism (the thing the previous attempt could not find)\n\nThere is NO render script and NO automation. `infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template` is rendered by a\nMANUAL OPERATOR STEP, and the recipe is documented in the template's own header (lines 4-12):\n\n    export REVIEW_BOT_PORT\n    envsubst '${REVIEW_BOT_PORT}' < infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template > /etc/nginx/conf.d/rebar.conf\n    nginx -t && systemctl reload nginx\n\nExactly ONE variable is templated: `${REVIEW_BOT_PORT}`. The single-quoted envsubst argument is\nload-bearing — it keeps nginx's own `$host` / `$remote_addr` / `$proxy_add_x_forwarded_for`\nuntouched. Copying the template verbatim is what produced the previous `unknown \"review_bot_port\"\nvariable` failure.\n\nValue: `REVIEW_BOT_PORT=8000`, single-sourced at `infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh:225`\n(`echo \"REVIEW_BOT_PORT=8000\"`) and by the compose default `${REVIEW_BOT_PORT:-8000}`\n(`infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:236`).\n\nPROVEN, not guessed — on the box, rendering the CHECKED-OUT (pre-fix) template with\n`REVIEW_BOT_PORT=8000` produced a file byte-identical to the live `/etc/nginx/conf.d/rebar.conf`:\n\n    diff /tmp/render_test.conf /etc/nginx/conf.d/rebar.conf  ->  IDENTICAL\n\nWhy nothing automates it: `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` deliberately never re-renders\n`conf.d/rebar.conf`. It only materialises the two GLOB-included files —\n`/etc/nginx/mcp-upstream.conf` (the blue-green upstream flip seam) and\n`/etc/nginx/opcert-guard*.conf` — and reloads nginx. So this manual install will NOT be reverted\nby autodeploy, and equally will NOT be applied to a rebuilt box automatically.\n\n## What was deployed\n\n- Backup: `/etc/nginx/conf.d/rebar.conf.pre-79b2-fix.1787868326.bak` (sha256 verified equal to the\n  pre-change live file: `baf0c908e45a...`).\n- Rendered `e9cec6bad8d1`'s template with `REVIEW_BOT_PORT=8000` -> 231 lines.\n- Pre-install sanity gate passed: >200 lines, contains `location = /mcp/`, contains\n  `Strict-Transport-Security`, contains `proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8000/;`, no unsubstituted `${`.\n- `nginx -t` exit code captured DIRECTLY (`nginx -t > out 2>&1; RC=$?`), not through a pipeline —\n  the previous attempt's `if nginx -t | tail -2; then` guard could never fail because a pipeline\n  reports `tail`'s status. RC=0, \"syntax is ok / test is successful\".\n- `nginx -s reload` RC=0, nginx `active`.\n\nDiff live->candidate was 86 lines and contained only this fix: the server-level HSTS `add_header`,\nthe two exact-match `location = /mcp/` and `location = /mcp` blocks proxying to\n`http://rebar_mcp/mcp`, and the three `proxy_redirect http://... https://...` pairs.\n\n## Live verification (from off-box)\n\nBEFORE: `GET /mcp/` -> `HTTP/2 307`, `location: http://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp`, no HSTS.\n\nAFTER:\n- `GET /mcp/`  -> 401, NO Location header at all, `strict-transport-security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains`\n- `POST /mcp/` -> 401, no Location, HSTS present (the real client verb; a 307 here is what would\n  have replayed method+body+bearer over plaintext)\n- `GET /mcp`   -> 401, unchanged, HSTS present\n- `/review/health` -> 200 + HSTS (review-bot intact, port 8000 rendering correct)\n- Gerrit `/` -> 200, `/login` -> 302 (intact)\n- `/opcert/` -> 403 (fail-closed deny-all, intact)\n- port 80 `/mcp/` -> 301 to https (intact)\n\nThe `www-authenticate` `resource_metadata` URL is https, as expected.\n\n## Live now vs awaiting merge\n\nLIVE NOW (manual install, this comment): part A (exact-match `/mcp/` + `/mcp` locations), part C\n(server-level HSTS with `always`), and the `proxy_redirect` backstop.\n\nSTILL AWAITING CHANGE 2280 MERGE: part B, `FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS=*` on the mcp compose service.\n`infra/compose/docker-compose.yml` IS in autodeploy's `MCP_PATHS`, so it deploys automatically on\nmerge via the blue-green path. The observed downgrade is gone without it, because nginx now maps\n`/mcp/` onto the app's `/mcp` so Starlette is never asked to redirect; part B remains needed as the\nforward-looking fix for absolute URLs the app builds from the request scheme.\n\nBecause the box's `/opt/rebar` checkout is at `d4a0a2a44` (pre-fix, 159-line template), the live\n`rebar.conf` is now AHEAD of the box's checkout. When 2280 merges, autodeploy will fast-forward the\ncheckout but will still not re-render nginx — the live file already carries the fix, so they\nconverge. Anyone who re-renders from the template after the merge gets the same bytes.\n\n## Deliberately not done\n\n- Did not touch change 2280 or merge anything; the nginx install is out-of-band by design and the\n  ticket's live-validation criterion is now evidenced.\n- Did not use any force override.\n- Pre-existing and NOT introduced here: `GET /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp` returns 404\n  (it falls through to the Gerrit `location /`). The config has no such location before OR after\n  this change — verified against the backup. Worth its own ticket; the MCP 401 advertises that URL.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787868522464445384,"uuid":"b65ba599-38f1-4c4d-a4b1-e5128ab0e11a"}